      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Labeo barbatus is a new import from the Congo. It grows to about 60 cm and is a representative of the genus Labeo, which is represented in the Congo River with at least 34 species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Fishes of this size and vivacity need very roomy aquariums and are not suitable for beginners.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Congo, Congo River.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In its habitat it lives in sections of strongly flowing water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Very roomy aquariums are needed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish usually place no high requirements on food and water chemistry, but they must be fed naturally and sufficiently, and the water filtered accordingly.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_barbatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Little is known about its behaviour in aquaria. Since Labeos generally become more aggressive with increasing age, a good aquarium structure is important: territory borders have to be offered and retreat areas created for suppressed individuals. Bogwood, stones, bamboo, plants etc. are suitable for this purpose.</p>"
    }
